{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/131841-inspirational-influential-mummy-media","id":131841,"title":"Inspirational/Influential Mummy Media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-11T01:18:31-07:00","id":131841,"title":"Inspirational/Influential Mummy Media","content":"Hi everybody,<br /> <br /> So I was thinking the other day about media (tv shows, movies,books, animation and music) to show to people to give them an idea of some of the themes and the general mood of Mummy the Curse. Obviously this sort of stuff was going to be in the Scroll of Ages, but since that never yielded anything I was thinking we could compile out own list here on the forums. <br /> <br /> I've got to admit the idea came from ArcaneArts mentioning inspirational media on another thread a while ago, who has in the past come up with several &quot;inspirational music&quot; threads across various boards on the Onyx Path Forum. <br /> <br /> As a little extra, I'm going to avoid the obvious choices like Brendan Fraiser's &quot;The Mummy&quot; movie series. Stuff with an Egyptian theme or historical setting is obviously fine and good. I'm looking primarily at media that resonates with the idea of a modern 21st century Mummy game. <br /> <br /> To get things started with an one of my favorites -<br /> <br /> <b>The Following</b> (TV Show) - A TV show all about an FBI agent (played by Kevin Bacon) history with and actions against a Cult run by a psychopathic ex-writer/professor. The main villain Carrol is much more a Slasher archetype then an Arisen parallel. However I think the way the cult is structured and its members act towards and defer to Carrol very much fit the idea of a Conspiracy Cult in Mummy. <br /> <br /> <b>The Jewel of Seven Stars</b> (Book) - A horror novel by Bram Stoker about cursed objects (and a Mummy's link to them), powerful magics, cults and the price of immortality. I'm pretty sure this was an influence on the later Mummy movies and through them on Mummy the Curse. <br /> <br /> <b>Les Friction</b> (Album/Band) - Don't know what it is about this album for me, but a lot of the songs and the themes/stories they allude to ring true for Mummy I feel. The juxtaposition of simple vocals with &quot;epic&quot; music styles (one of the bands members if the remaining member of E.S. Posthumous) just really works for Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T01:25:44-07:00","id":131869,"title":"","content":"History books. Pretty much all of them. Mummy is a fantastic game for bringing history back to life, giving mummy characters historic backgrounds and flashbacks, having them witness significant moments in history. History itself is the greatest inspiration for Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T01:48:50-07:00","id":131904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/131841-inspirational-influential-mummy-media#post131841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The Jewel of Seven Stars</b> (Book) - A horror novel by Bram Stoker about cursed objects (and a Mummy's link to them), powerful magics, cults and the price of immortality. I'm pretty sure this was an influence on the later Mummy movies and through them on Mummy the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven Stars is a bit of a slow burn. In Mummy the Curse, Corbeck would have already been slaughtered by the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T01:54:13-07:00","id":131922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/131841-inspirational-influential-mummy-media?p=131904#post131904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seven Stars is a bit of a slow burn. In Mummy the Curse, Corbeck would have already been slaughtered by the Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. However, the media listed in this thread is not 1:1 Mummy the Curse compatible, just media that can clue people into aspects of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:11:20-07:00","id":132155,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/hieroglyph-first-cast-photo-702664\" target=\"_blank\">This</a><br /> <br /> Scheduled for 13 episodes, sort of riding on the coat-tails of Vikings on History channel. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:13:48-07:00","id":132157,"title":"","content":"The Noah movie from earlier in the year is one that I find an interesting source of inspiration (even if, as a film, I had pretty mixed feelings towards it). The first is on a count of aesthetics. The intriguing apocalyptic/industrial/stone age mash-up of the ruined human outposts has a fascinating air of primitive technology that I think can be co-opted and spiced with some ancient Egyptian flavour. Irem isn't just a proto-Egypt, after all, but a civilisation that was simultaneously more advanced and more primitive than its successors, and I think the Noah movie gave a good shot of capturing what that combination might look like.<br /> <br /> The second is on the more personal level, in how Noah interacts with the Creator in the film, which I think works as a good idea of how a Mummy might interact with their Judge. The messages aren't spoken words, but instead impressions, feelings, and the occasional vision in need of interpretation. The God in the film feels unknowable and a little bit alien (not to mention Judging humanity for their crimes and exacting a brutal retribution), which is almost exactly like the Judges. And just like the Judges, the Creator asks Noah to undertake tasks that, from the point of view of human mortality, are downright heinous. But the whole while, Noah can't be entirely sure how much of what he is doing is down to divine mandate, and how much the Creator has left up to his own judgement. For a Mummy in the same situation, do you lean towards barbarism because the Judges seem to prefer that, or do you struggle to maintain your morality when not bowing to the will of the divine being guiding you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T13:44:52-07:00","id":132757,"title":"","content":"Doctor Who: might be a little hit and miss for how an impossibly old person form a superior culture interacts with the people. Not to mention all the cult like organizations, motivations and ideologies that crop up. And season 7's The Rings of Akhaten has a wonderful space mummy.<br /> <br /> Stargate is loaded with false gods and near immortals, often playing off an Egyptian theme. and the high tech Relics that abound through out the series.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T16:23:33-07:00","id":154255,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten DC yet (I know what's wrong with me?) so I don't know much yet, but I've been watching Alpha House on Amazon Prime and it kind of resembles a mummy society in a very weird way. It's about 4 senators and their experiences working in American politics. The senators are the mummies, very powerful but also old and out of touch with a lot of things. They all have a group of loyal assistants (I forget their actual job title) that act as the high priest/ess for their mummy lords and keep them in line.<br /> <br /> If you want to focus on a political angle for your mummy game, this might be a good place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","user":"RisTigger","date":". 05-30-2014, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:19:23-08:00","id":371576,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necro, but these threads are always useful. I can suggest the <i>Casca</i> series, an old line of novels about Longinus (the spearman who stabbed Jesus on the cross); he's cursed to fight as a soldier until the time of Reckoning. It's a lot of fun to look at a soldier who has been fighting since the time of Rome, and his take on WW2 or Vietnam. A great look at how jaded an immortal can become regarding their own fate, even if his Memory is high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:27:53-08:00","id":371587,"title":"","content":"Has no one mentioned Planescape: Torment yet?<br /> <br /> Because if ever there were a great example of the complications caused by Memory, it's Planescape: Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}